<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>TechTeaStudio.Billing</PackageId>
    <!-- Must be a literal tag in this file - the publish workflow greps for it. Keep in sync
         with TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions.csproj; see the note in Directory.Build.props. -->
    <Version>0.5.3</Version>
    <Description>Provider-agnostic payment billing for ASP.NET Core. Hosted checkout and verified webhooks for Stripe, YooKassa, Shopify and Telegram Stars, plus external donation platforms (Ko-fi, Patreon, manual Boosty) with claim-code attribution and an unclaimed-purchase holding area - all behind one IBillingProvider seam with pluggable payment store and fulfillment. Targets net5.0 through net10.0.</Description>
    <PackageTags>billing;payments;stripe;yookassa;shopify;telegram;kofi;patreon;boosty;donations;checkout;webhook;aspnetcore;TechTeaStudio</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v0.5.3: TelegramStarsBillingProvider can mint invoice LINKS (Bot API createInvoiceLink) via ITelegramBot.CreateInvoiceLinkAsync - the payment sheet opens directly, no bot chat and no /start. The deep-link flow only shows START to a user who never started the bot; a returning user got a silent chat and no invoice.

v0.5.0: TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions additionally targets netstandard2.0 and net472, so .NET Framework 4.6.2+ assemblies can share the contracts. This package itself stays .NET 5+ - it needs the ASP.NET Core shared framework, which has not run on .NET Framework since ASP.NET Core 3.0.

v0.4.0: Targets net5.0 through net10.0 (was net8.0+). Contracts split into the dependency-free TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions package, pulled in automatically - namespaces are unchanged, so existing code compiles as-is. Webhook endpoints now map through RequestDelegate instead of minimal-API lambdas, which is what makes net5.0/net6.0 possible; behaviour and status codes are identical. Symbol packages, SourceLink and package validation added.

Full changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Billing/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions\TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions\TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
